  "query_preview": "through the weekend.\n\nLate tonight and early Thursday morning, there is a low probability \nfor isolated showers in north-central KS where there may be some \nisentropic ascent. Have kept POPs less than 15 percent for now given \nthe low confidence of any measurable precipitation, supported by \nweak forcing a lack of saturation in the column. Instead, heat will\ncontinue and be reinforced as the mid-level ridge builds westward \nover the central CONUS this weekend and holds firm into next week. A \nbit of relief may arrive during the middle of next week as long range\nmodels show the ridge flattening and a possible cold front moving \nthrough the area by late week. The EC is more set on this solution \nthan the GFS currently, even bringing some decent QPF with the front.\nWe will have to watch how models trend in the long range, but for \nnow, confidence remains high in dry and very hot weather for at \nleast the next week.",
